 known as Gray Television, Inc. and changed its name to Gray Media, Inc. in July 2002. Gray Media, Inc. was founded in 1891 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Hilton Hatchett Howell Jr. | Executive Chairman & CEO | Age 63 | Compensation: $4.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $338K ranks in the bottom quartile among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 18%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Gray Media, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $617M market cap on $3.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +18% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $181M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 7.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the 