gh to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 61% in the 2020 crash, 63% in the 2022 bear market and 98% in 2008."],"val":["The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 74%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Communication Services peers: P/FCF 3.4 vs 11.1 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 39% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 29.3% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 5.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 5 covering analysts target $6.60 on average, 10% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 4% falls short of the cost of capital of 7.0%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.40).","It converts 6% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is a concern: a weak Piotroski score of 3/9 and cash conversion of only -3.40x.","It spends 0.7% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 8.5x net debt to EBITDA ($368.0M of cash against $5.7B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 0.8x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 0.65 in the distress zone."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -5.6% over 3 years, 5.4% over 5 years and 17.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 29%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded -19.7% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 31%.","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (3.5% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 11, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 7.1%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 82%.","It returns 5.3% a year to shareholders (5.3% in dividends).","The share count has grown 5.8% a year over five years, diluting